  {
   "id": 422973,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Michael Koenigs’ group in 2008 initiated a large-scale study to determine if abnormal activity in the different regions of the prefrontal cortex contributes to the emotional symptoms common to depression. The results of this study indicate:",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 927045,
     "content_html": "participants with ventromedial prefrontal cortex damage were diagnosed with little or no depression on the BDI."
    },
    {
     "id": 927046,
     "content_html": "participants with dorsolateral prefrontal cortex damage displayed high levels of depression on the BDI scale."
    },
    {
     "id": 927047,
     "content_html": "ventromedial prefrontal cortex damaged participants displayed high levels of depression d. dorsolateral prefrontal cortex damaged participants show little or no depression"
    },
    {
     "id": 927048,
     "content_html": "Only a and b"
    }
   ],
